// The shape of a `.html` view file: the blocks it is made of, recovered as
// RAW SOURCE TEXT with the offsets they came from.
//
// Split out of `viewgen/` because two very different consumers need it and
// only one of them is a code generator. `viewgen` slices a file in order to
// EMIT MoonBit; `tutucard` slices the same file in order to RUN it, in a
// browser, with no generator anywhere in the payload. A runtime that had to
// import an emitter to find out where the templates are would be carrying the
// whole `emit_*` layer for the sake of a tokenizer loop.
//
// Pure and target-agnostic like `statedef` and `viewgen`: source text in,
// typed blocks out, never touching the filesystem.
//
// It parses the state and init blocks and does NOT parse the script block,
// and that asymmetry is deliberate rather than unfinished — see `ViewFile`.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/statedef",
  "moonbit-community/html/src" @html5,
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
}
